Error [E0003]: `take_pattern` takes a literal pattern string, not the name `pat`
  --> tests/ui/take_pattern_computed_arg.jet:6:25
    |
  6 |     m :: c.take_pattern(pat) ?? panic("no match")
    |                         ^^^
 Why: The pattern is matched at compile time, so it must be written directly as a string literal
 Fix: Write `take_pattern("literal-{hole}-pattern")` or `take_pattern([U8]{"…"})` for bytes
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0003
